# CODEOWNERS
# Defines who must review changes to specific files/directories.
# These owners are automatically requested for review on PRs.
# Format: <pattern> <GitHub-username(s)>
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Global default owner (catches everything not listed below)
* @your-github-username

# CI/CD and infrastructure — highest scrutiny
.github/                    @your-github-username
.clinerules                  @your-github-username
.clinerules.d/secrets.md     @your-github-username
.gitleaks.toml               @your-github-username

# Environment configuration — no changes without owner review
.env.example                 @your-github-username
src/config/                  @your-github-username

# Database schema — migrations are irreversible
src/db/migrations/           @your-github-username

# Security-sensitive areas
src/auth/                    @your-github-username
src/middleware/               @your-github-username

# Documentation
docs/                        @your-github-username
README.md                    @your-github-username
CHANGELOG.md                 @your-github-username
